sidebar(
# Aeon Divinities

Whether the aeons serve an actual divinity, a philosophical concept, or merely a
"supreme oneness" is a topic hotly debated by planar scholars.

Most aeons care little for the question, pursuing their inscrutable duties across
the multiverse without pause or complaint.
)

More body text continues after the first sidebar, flowing down the column and
giving the layout additional prose to paginate around the callout boxes that sit
within the page's normal two-column text.

sidebar(
# Draconic Groupings

Dragons are loosely sorted by temperament and by the planes they call home:

* Metallic dragons, often protective
* Chromatic dragons, often cruel
* Primal dragons, tied to the planes

| Age      | Size  |
| -------- | ----- |
| Wyrmling | Small |
| Adult    | Large |
| Ancient  | Huge  |
)

